  "body": "consider:\r\n\r\n```webidl\r\n\r\nenum A {\r\n  \"foo\",\r\n  \"bar\"\r\n};\r\n\r\nenum B {\r\n  \"foo\",\r\n  \"baz\"\r\n};\r\n\r\ninterface C {\r\n  attribute (A or B) prop;\r\n};\r\n```\r\n\r\nwhat happens if we do `someC.prop = \"foo\"`?\r\n\r\nI think probably we should just disallow union types where the flattened member types contain enums with conflicting values.",
